scripts/
docs/
workers/
tenants/*/config.js
# ...except OSA's, which is not a legacy fallback but the portal's only
# source of CLEARSKY_CONFIG. tenants/osa/portfolio.html boots by polling
# for that global and retrying every 120 ms until it appears, so with the
# file excluded the page spins on "Loading portfolio..." forever — no
# error, no timeout, nothing in the console. The blanket pattern came in
# with the 16-repo consolidation and took this one with it by accident.
# It carries no secrets: the Firebase web config is public by design, and
# the commercial fields (defaultFeeBasis, closedUsdPerYear) are empty.
!tenants/osa/config.js
tenants/*/*.rules
tenants/*/*.md
*.md
!tenants/osa/*.md

# ── NOT WEB CONTENT, AND ONE OF THEM IS THE CUSTOMER BOOK ────────────────
# Vercel serves the repo root, so anything sitting here is a URL. These were:
#
#   /firestore.rules       200 — the entire access-control model, comments and
#   /storage.rules         200   all, including which collections are called
#                                out as the most sensitive and why. Rules are
#                                enforced server-side so secrecy is not the
#                                control, but handing an attacker the map and
#                                the reasoning is still a gift.
#   /admin/seed-plan.json  200 — every tenant's name, domain, hostname and
#                                billing tier in one file at a guessable path.
#                                That is the customer list.
#   /firebase.json         200 — harmless, but it is CLI config, not a page.
#
# seed-plan.json is fetched by the console's one-shot "seed tenants" button.
# omega_orgs is already seeded, so that button is spent; if it is ever needed
# again, regenerate the file and deploy without this line for one release.
firestore.rules
storage.rules
firestore.indexes.json
firebase.json
admin/seed-plan.json

# ── SERVERLESS SOURCE SITTING IN THE STATIC TREE ─────────────────────────
# Found 2026-09-17 by scripts/steward/guard.js. Vercel only treats /api at
# the project root as functions; every other copy of a function is a static
# file, and the root serves the repo, so each of these was a 200:
#
#   /grid-atlas.js            the Grid Atlas scoring model, weights and all
#   /render.js                the render pipeline
#   /commercial.js            the C&I source adapter (no api/ copy exists —
#                             it has never been deployed as a function)
#   /api-crm-sync.js          the CRM proxy, whose whole point is that it is
#                             the ONLY place CRM credentials live
#   /tenants/osa/**           OSA's copies of score and grid-atlas
#   /portals/finance/**       the finance portal's copy of omega-ai-extract
#
# None of them holds a secret — they read process.env at runtime — and none
# is referenced by a <script src> anywhere in the repo, so excluding them
# changes no behaviour. What they hold is the logic CLAUDE.md puts in /api/
# precisely so it is not downloadable. The api/ copies keep running.
#
# ⚠ THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. .vercelignore takes .gitignore
# semantics, where a pattern with no slash matches AT EVERY DEPTH — so a bare
# `grid-atlas.js` excluded api/grid-atlas.js too, and `render.js` took
# api/render.js with it. vercel.json names both of those in `functions`, so
# the build failed outright:
#
#     The pattern "api/grid-atlas.js" defined in `functions`
#     doesn't match any Serverless Functions.
#
# That failure was the lucky outcome. Without those two entries in
# vercel.json the deploy would have SUCCEEDED and quietly shipped without the
# Grid Atlas and render endpoints — the exact opposite of "the api/ copies
# keep running". Anchored to the root, which is what was meant.
/grid-atlas.js
/render.js
/commercial.js
/api-crm-sync.js
tenants/osa/score.js
tenants/osa/api/score.js
tenants/osa/api/grid-atlas.js
portals/finance/omega-ai-extract.js
portals/finance/api/omega-ai-extract.js
